WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.020 --> 00:00:06.900
I’ve had a long interest in physics and
math ever since middle school.

00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:12.940
But, I was discouraged to choose these two
as my major when I went to college.

00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:19.030
And that’s because my family thought that
I would have a hard time to find a job

00:00:19.030 --> 00:00:25.019
with this major as a female, based on what
we saw at that time in China.

00:00:25.019 --> 00:00:31.180
So instead I chose Biology as my major and
it opened a new door for me.

00:00:31.180 --> 00:00:36.940
It actually provided the foundation for my
current research and it also lead me to a

00:00:36.940 --> 00:00:42.160
beautiful world of evolution and life science.

00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:47.079
For my Ph.D., I chose computational biology
because

00:00:47.079 --> 00:00:53.700
it is a major that combines my passion in
computation and my interest in biology.

00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:57.610
For a long time I observed that for computer
scientists, if they wanted to

00:00:57.610 --> 00:01:03.090
understand biomedical data they needed to
have a good understanding of biology.

00:01:03.090 --> 00:01:08.660
For biologists, if they wanted to speed the
discovery they required the help of computer scientists.

00:01:08.660 --> 00:01:11.899
And my background sort of bridged this gap.

00:01:11.899 --> 00:01:17.740
I think we’re at a great stage where we
can actually have the ability to turn data

00:01:17.740 --> 00:01:23.749
into actionable items that can be directly
applied to medical decision making.

00:01:23.749 --> 00:01:29.340
Data science and the microbiome combined to
improve our health

00:01:29.340 --> 00:01:35.700
NLM is one of the few places where I can start
my research program in data science.

00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:42.679
There is a critical mass of truly exceptional
and top-notch scientists here.

00:01:42.679 --> 00:01:46.349
And I also found people in NLM are approachable.

00:01:46.349 --> 00:01:49.649
From the director to the top scientist,

00:01:49.649 --> 00:01:55.429
you can just knock on their door and talk
with them and they are always willing to help.

00:01:55.429 --> 00:02:01.259
NLM is the place where I can do the research
that I love and enjoy

00:02:01.260 --> 00:02:04.000
and also make a difference at the same time.

